          "description": "Auto-assign the ticket to the next agent in round-robin order by ascending AGENT_ID among Active agents whose PREFERENCE matches CATEGORY",
          "spec": "After a new ticket is committed (action = add) with no ASSIGNED_AGENT yet: find all SUPPORT360_AGENT rows where AGENT_STATUS = 'Active' and PREFERENCE equals the ticket's CATEGORY. Ignore AGENT_AVAILABILITY entirely \u2014 it is never checked. If no Active agent matches, leave STATUS = 'Pending' and ASSIGNED_AGENT empty. If one or more match, assign round-robin by ascending AGENT_ID: look up the most recently created ticket in SUPPORT360_TICKET (by CREATED_DATE descending, excluding this ticket) where CATEGORY equals this ticket's CATEGORY and ASSIGNED_AGENT is not empty. If found, pick the first matching Active agent (ordered ascending by AGENT_ID) whose AGENT_ID is strictly greater than that previous ticket's ASSIGNED_AGENT; if none is greater, wrap around to the matching agent with the lowest AGENT_ID. If no prior assigned ticket exists for that category, pick the matching agent with the lowest AGENT_ID. Set ASSIGNED_AGENT to that agent's AGENT_ID and STATUS = 'Assigned'. Never set STATUS to 'Queued' \u2014 that status is no longer used. Log the assignment to SUPPORT360_TICKET_ACTLOG. Never blocks the save."
        }
      }
